{
  "description": "key = splitmix64(seed_n + fnv1a64(32 ASCII bytes of the canonical ID)); sort by key ascending as UNSIGNED 64-bit, ties by the ID bytes ascending (unsigned, byte by byte). 'derived' cases compute keys from a seed and an epoch; 'sortCases' give the keys directly, so the unsigned comparison and the tie-break are tested on their own (a tie of derived keys needs an FNV collision, which is not practical to find). The same function gives the key of a group for randomInOrder (the group's canonical ID is hashed). Published here; the scheduler (F1.1) implements and runs it. Every 64-bit value is an object: dec (unsigned decimal string), hex (16 lower-case digits, no prefix), hi and lo (its high and low 32 bits as 8 lower-case hex digits), so a port without a native 64-bit integer can check each step.",
